 "readme": "# Auriga-SBI\n\n[![Paper](https://img.shields.io/badge/Paper-DOI%3A10.1093%2Fmnras%2Fstaf1343-blue)](https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/staf1343)\n\n## Overview\n\n`auriga-sbi` is a research repository for simulation-based inference (SBI) on the Auriga cosmological galaxy simulations. It contains data preparation, generative model training, and inference pipelines designed to infer merger and accretion parameters for progenitor histories in simulated Milky Way-like galaxies using a variety of different methods (in different branches). \n\nThe repository also includes a completed analysis and results summary in `paper.pdf`.\n\n## Files overview\n\n- `create_dataframe_sbi.py`: build and prepare dataframe datasets for SBI training and evaluation.\n- `sbi_model_final.py`: final data-processing and training pipeline for the main SBI inference workflow.\n- `training.py`: training utilities and functions for inference models.\n- `get_results.py`: validation utilities and functions for inference models.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Gain access to the Auriga simulations following instructions [here](https://wwwmpa.mpa-garching.mpg.de/auriga/data.html).\n2. Place the repository in your working environment.\n3. Install required Python packages using:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n3. Update any local data paths in the scripts if necessary. Many workflows currently reference absolute paths to local datasets and may need adjustment for your environment.\n\n4. Extract merger-debris pairs from the simulaitons using a `submitCPU.sh`\n\n5. Train SBI models and run validation tests as in `submitGPU.sh`\n\nEach script defines its own command-line arguments and defaults, so inspect the file for available options.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Dependencies are managed in `requirements.txt`.\n- The repo relies on local datasets.\n- `paper.pdf` contains the written analysis and presentation of results associated with this work.\n\n\n",
